# Planner consumer #1 — bare-param mutation in a top-level `for … else:` ELSE
# body (a range shape, which the self-host DOES lower). Distinct from the 2G
# fixture `cow_loop_bare_param_for_else` (a for-else nested inside a while): here
# the for loop's OWN pre-header scan is extended to fold in the else body. `for …
# else` is OUT of the ggdef phase-0 subset, so this lives in known_gaps/ and is
# validated on the two production backends only: C=3,4 and LLVM=3,4 (pre-fix both
# printed 4,4). SH note: SH for-else is implemented for range/set (not
# Vector/Dict); the range shape here is SH-supported and the whole-fn suffix
# scan reaches the else body.
void f(Vector[int] xs):
    for i in 0..1:
        pass
    else:
        xs.pop()
    print(xs.len())

void main():
    Vector[int] a = [1, 2, 3, 4]
    f(a)
    print(a.len())
